      "## 05/09/2026 17:18 — YouTube Audio Eraser\n\nPartner, the **“Audio eraser — YouTube”** shown at the top of your Samsung Quick Panel means **Samsung’s Audio Eraser feature is currently available/active for the YouTube audio you’re playing**.\n\nAudio Eraser is a Galaxy AI audio feature that can reduce particular types of sound in a video/audio, such as **voices, music, wind, crowd/background noise, and other unwanted sounds**, while keeping the sounds you want.\n\nSo **it isn't a YouTube feature or separate YouTube app**. Samsung detected YouTube playing media and is offering its **Audio Eraser** processing for that media.\n\nFor example, if you're watching a YouTube video where somebody is talking but there is loud background music, Audio Eraser can potentially **turn down the music/background sound and make the voice clearer**.\n\nThe interesting thing in your screenshot is that Samsung is exposing it **directly in the Quick Panel while YouTube is the active media source**. If you tap **“Audio eraser”**, I can explain exactly what each option you see does."
